{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper","id":891067,"title":"C20: Wonder, Seeker, Keeper?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-15T03:29:43-07:00","id":891067,"title":"C20: Wonder, Seeker, Keeper?","content":"I was catching up on the C20 teasers and reading the Nocker write-up and it seems super cool. Though one thing worries me a little - are they totally changing the Childling, Wilder, Grump set-up? What are the new categories of Wonder, Seeker, Keeper, and will they be age-bound as they used to be? That certainly seemed to be the dominant perspective in the comments. <br /> <br /> Let me preface this by saying my excitement remains undiminished, I'm so thrilled we're getting this book. I don't want to be negative and I'm well aware that this is speculation and that execution can make a big difference. <br /> <br /> That said, if they are moving away from the age-related categories and the focus on how growing older and banality are tied together, I think I'd be sad. To me, in many ways, Changeling is a story about growing up, growing older, working out how to do that without letting the world kill you. There's a poignancy to the way the Dreaming allows you to live forever while the mortal world makes you live with the desperation of Logan's Run. One of the things that is truly unique about Changeling is the position children occupy in society and the fact that playing child characters is detailed and given space and attention. <br /> <br /> I've definitely seen players talk about how having childlings in a game can make it more difficult to explain - why is this 20 year old hanging out with this 11 year old? But it was never a perspective I shared - to me, well, that's sort of the point. How <i>do</i> you explain that? If you have to stop taking the 11 year old with you on adventures, is that a banal decision on your part? Does it have a banal effect on the Childling? How - as an adult - do you feel about taking children on adventures to start with? What if the kid has a Remembrance of 5 and is more capable than you as a warrior? What if the kid doesn't but has been chosen by the Dreaming for a quest? What if neither of those is true, but the terrors and wonders of the Dreaming keeps the child's soul alive and the other option is the crushing banality of being a bullied kid at school with Autumn People for parents? <br /> <br /> I guess I just think these are really cool questions, and the notion that, inevitably, banality increases with age, is a really core part of the game. I'm not sure how I'll feel if you can just say &quot;Sure, I'm 30, but I'm young at heart!&quot; and choose Childling stats? <br /> <br /> I don't know. As I said, I certainly am not trying to make an assumption about what will ultimately be in the book. But based on the comments in the thread, it seemed like a lot of people had a really different opinion to me on what I consider to be a really key feature of the game. So I guess I'm just asking about that. <br /> <br /> Am I the only one who would be sad to see this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T05:32:13-07:00","id":891095,"title":"","content":"For me, the problem is the names. They're just dull. A better option (for me) would be to keep age-related Seemings and have Wonder, Seeker and Keeper as a kind of status or rank, instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:33:12-07:00","id":891141,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've always been ambivalent about age being linked to Seeming. On the one hand it reinforces the idea of Changeling as a game about being young, which I've always mined a lot out of. On the other hand I don't love the infantilism that tends to come with viewing &quot;growing up&quot; as wrong. What I have experimented with in the past is making Childling, Wilder, and Grump less about innate Glamour and Banality and more about the ease with which one gathers Glamour versus the resistance one has to Banality. <br /> <br /> Then again I was already playing Grumps when I was a Wilder. For me Grump is where Changeling really begins, everything else is just prelude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T12:31:58-07:00","id":891315,"title":"","content":"There are children who grow up too fast, and adults who never do. There are plenty of people the category system just doesn't work for based on age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:34:51-07:00","id":891375,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> - I like the names as they are because they're a little weird and awkward, but can see that others might not. I wouldn't have a problem if it was essentially a name change. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> - I think where we differ is that I don't see it as saying that growing up is wrong, I think it's focusing on a specific type of pressure that comes with growing up. For instance I don't think taking responsibility for your actions, fighting for what you believe in or protecting those you love - all aspects of growing up - are portrayed negatively in the game. What I think it focuses on is the way that as you grow up - and specifically as you go from being a child to a young adult to a regular adult (i.e. that sweep from childhood through to your late twenties) - society expects different things of you and gives you progressively less leeway for nonconformism. Obviously there are children suffering under incredibly banal conditions just as there are adults lucky enough to live lives in places and with people who exert far less pressure. No system is going to be perfect for every occasion. But very broadly speaking, the values of imagination, play and whimsy are progressively less valued as you &quot;grow up&quot;. So...for <i>that</i> value of growing up, I think that Changeling does take a position that &quot;growing up&quot; is wrong, but I'm not sure I'd view it as infantilism. You know, for <i>that </i>definition of growing up. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> I spoke about this some in my original post. I also think it's worth pointing to the paragraph above to define my view on what CtD means by &quot;growing up is bad&quot;, but based on that, the fight against banality and its inevitable ultimate victory is - to me - the very core of the game and what makes it both beautiful and sad. No system will fit every character all the time (and I'd argue that it's completely possible to represent a Grump who is on the edge of the Forgetting versus one who is vibrant and joyful and fully awake in the Dreaming with the mechanics we already have), but to say that the core conflict of the game just...doesn't affect you because you're &quot;young at heart&quot; and chose not to grow up? I mean, the <i>entire game</i> is about struggling to make that choice. So - mitigated, as <i>everything</i> should be, by the golden rule - I still feel quite firmly that Changeling's focus on...not necessarily age, but the process of ageing, is really interesting and a really huge part of the game. <br /> <br /> Even if others don't agree with my specific take on why the current agebound system is valuable, I guess I'd still say that this is a really big change to the system. Like a really huge setting change, and I suppose...my preference would be for the 20th anniversary edition to be the definitive edition of a game I've loved for two decades rather than a place to experiment with large changes to the setting. <br /> <br /> Again, to reiterate, I make no assumptions about what they are doing, and if they make a change like this that I dislike, it will be easy enough to houserule. But yeah. That's where I'm at with it conceptually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:33:38-07:00","id":891411,"title":"","content":"If I'm reading between the lines correctly--and it's a very real possibility that I'm not--then both the childling, wilder, grump <i>and</i> the wonder, seeker, keeper setup will be used simultaneously for characters. The age category (childling, etc) will likely be used to determine a character's age and their inherent banality vs glamour, whereas the lifestyles category (wonder, etc) will be used to determine a character's interactions with others and likely how they gather glamour. Note the description of the Nocker's attitudes are all about their relationship to knowledge. The Eshu write-up will likely be about their relationship to stories, the Boggan write-up will likely focus on their relationship to work. <br /> <br /> The nocker wonder reads like they would gather glamour from going out and learning mechanical skills and taking things apart, i.e. by engaging in their curiosity about machines they gain glamour. So too with the other lifestyles. And these don't really have to preclude the childling, wilder, or grump age categories.<br /> <br /> That's my guess at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:51:05-07:00","id":891422,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11658_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11658\" data-vbnamecard=\"11658\">Rabbit Pooka</a> I hope you're reading correctly - I think that would be a really cool additional mechanic that would add to the current set up rather than undermining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:58:01-07:00","id":891535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=891375#post891375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> I spoke about this some in my original post. I also think it's worth pointing to the paragraph above to define my view on what CtD means by &quot;growing up is bad&quot;, but based on that, the fight against banality and its inevitable ultimate victory is - to me - the very core of the game and what makes it both beautiful and sad. No system will fit every character all the time (and I'd argue that it's completely possible to represent a Grump who is on the edge of the Forgetting versus one who is vibrant and joyful and fully awake in the Dreaming with the mechanics we already have), but to say that the core conflict of the game just...doesn't affect you because you're &quot;young at heart&quot; and chose not to grow up? I mean, the <i>entire game</i> is about struggling to make that choice. So - mitigated, as <i>everything</i> should be, by the golden rule - I still feel quite firmly that Changeling's focus on...not necessarily age, but the process of ageing, is really interesting and a really huge part of the game.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel its the central conflict of the game. Balancing Dream vs Real Life is. Maturity and what one chooses to do with it is not an age thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T02:21:30-07:00","id":891634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=891535#post891535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't feel its the central conflict of the game. Balancing Dream vs Real Life is. Maturity and what one chooses to do with it is not an age thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I ever suggested maturity had anything to do with it? I spent quite a while discussing this with Primogen Caitiff explaining I thought there were many aspects of &quot;growing up&quot; that were beneficial - taking responsibility for one's actions, protecting what you love, fighting for the things you believe in, to name a few. Maturity is not banal. <br /> <br /> The specific <i>form</i> of growing up CtD portrays as negative is the increasing pressure to conform, to prioritise &quot;real life&quot; over &quot;dreaming&quot;. And that is something for which social pressure increases as you travel from childhood into adulthood. Even if specific individuals have lives where that is not the case, the effect would still be cumulative, and the longer you exist in opposition to the external forces of banality, the more they will affect you. <br /> <br /> Age may not be a thing for an individual, but it is <i>very</i> much a thing in terms of societal expectation. <br /> <br /> The fact that Changelings often lead brief, brilliant lives is underscored by the mechanical reminder that, for most, you are living on borrowed time. I maintain that if the the core theme of Changeling is the struggle to stay in the Dreaming and fight against the Forgetting for as long as possible - however we choose to define those sides of the coin - then decoupling the likelihood of the Forgetting from the age of the character represents a very large shift in the game's setting (whether we view that positively or negatively), and also, in my mind, rather defangs the Forgetting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:50:31-07:00","id":892146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=891411#post891411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm reading between the lines correctly--and it's a very real possibility that I'm not--then both the childling, wilder, grump <i>and</i> the wonder, seeker, keeper setup will be used simultaneously for characters. The age category (childling, etc) will likely be used to determine a character's age and their inherent banality vs glamour, whereas the lifestyles category (wonder, etc) will be used to determine a character's interactions with others and likely how they gather glamour. Note the description of the Nocker's attitudes are all about their relationship to knowledge. The Eshu write-up will likely be about their relationship to stories, the Boggan write-up will likely focus on their relationship to work. <br /> <br /> The nocker wonder reads like they would gather glamour from going out and learning mechanical skills and taking things apart, i.e. by engaging in their curiosity about machines they gain glamour. So too with the other lifestyles. And these don't really have to preclude the childling, wilder, or grump age categories.<br /> <br /> That's my guess at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one of the writers (Pooka Knight?) has hinted at this as well. It makes sense, I guess. I mean, we know there's going to be a new way to reap Glamour (Revelry), so perhaps this is tied to that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:44:34-07:00","id":892182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892146#post892146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least one of the writers (Pooka Knight?) has hinted at this as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dropped a few hints about seemings in one of my play test write ups, but things do change. There are some things changing in direct response to play tests, and some of the original ideas in the first drafts might be a step too far for a 20th Anniversary book.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to say more, but I'm afraid I'll get myself in trouble for revealing anything too early. I can't wait for this book to get in everyone's hands so we can talk about it openly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T21:42:22-07:00","id":892266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=891634#post891634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I ever suggested maturity had anything to do with it? I spent quite a while discussing this with Primogen Caitiff explaining I thought there were many aspects of &quot;growing up&quot; that were beneficial - taking responsibility for one's actions, protecting what you love, fighting for the things you believe in, to name a few. Maturity is not banal.<br /> <br /> The specific <i>form</i> of growing up CtD portrays as negative is the increasing pressure to conform, to prioritise &quot;real life&quot; over &quot;dreaming&quot;. And that is something for which social pressure increases as you travel from childhood into adulthood. Even if specific individuals have lives where that is not the case, the effect would still be cumulative, and the longer you exist in opposition to the external forces of banality, the more they will affect you.<br /> <br /> Age may not be a thing for an individual, but it is <i>very</i> much a thing in terms of societal expectation.<br /> <br /> The fact that Changelings often lead brief, brilliant lives is underscored by the mechanical reminder that, for most, you are living on borrowed time. I maintain that if the the core theme of Changeling is the struggle to stay in the Dreaming and fight against the Forgetting for as long as possible - however we choose to define those sides of the coin - then decoupling the likelihood of the Forgetting from the age of the character represents a very large shift in the game's setting (whether we view that positively or negatively), and also, in my mind, rather defangs the Forgetting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Race and economics have as much of an effect on social expectations along with well location, being able to better model more of the human condition for the conflict between Dream and Mundanity is a good thing. Your interpretation no offense intended comes off as &quot;The horror of White suburbia&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T04:57:14-07:00","id":892425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892266#post892266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Race and economics have as much of an effect on social expectations along with well location, being able to better model more of the human condition for the conflict between Dream and Mundanity is a good thing. Your interpretation no offense intended comes off as &quot;The horror of White suburbia&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree that the intersectional issues of race, poverty, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, etc., are likely to impact on someone's social status and - in Changeling terms - the amount of banality they are likely to face. <br /> <br /> I disagree that that is relevant to the very broad statement that, in addition to any individual factors, most societies, and groups within society, have increased expectations of their members as they grow into adulthood. There is an increased expectation to conform to social norms. <br /> <br /> Respectfully, if you think I'm describing &quot;the horror of white suburbia&quot; I suspect that may be down to your assumptions more than anything I said. I also think that's a criticism that could plausibly be discussed with regards to the original game. Changeling is extraordinarily close to my heart, but in retrospect, while well-meaning, it is quite focused on white, Western urban fantasy of a particular genre. The Eshu, for instance, could be validly read as kind of tokenistic. <br /> <br /> But to return to what I've actually been describing - if specifics would help - when we're talking about pressure to conform, I don't just mean the expectation to get a nine to five job and do your taxes on time. I also mean the crippling <i>need</i> to work three jobs because if you don't your family will starve. I also mean mandatory military service. I also mean the way young boys are trained to shut down their feelings and encouraged to express themselves with aggression. I also mean the way police officers are trained to dehumanise black children. <br /> <br /> And ultimately, even if we were to agree and decide that the amount of banality leveled against adults and children was the same (and in some situations that will be the case, or the reverse will even be true), it is <i>cumulative</i>. The longer you live, the longer you have been fighting, the more it will wound you. <br /> <br /> It comes back to the fact that Changeling, since the beginning, has focused on the fact that changelings know they may very well have <i>brief</i> lives. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I think representing that with age is fairer than doing so with any other attribute, because unlike race, gender, economic status, etc., aging is universal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T05:01:35-07:00","id":892428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892182#post892182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dropped a few hints about seemings in one of my play test write ups, but things do change. There are some things changing in direct response to play tests, and some of the original ideas in the first drafts might be a step too far for a 20th Anniversary book.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to say more, but I'm afraid I'll get myself in trouble for revealing anything too early. I can't wait for this book to get in everyone's hands so we can talk about it openly!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome, thanks for the information. I'm glad to hear that the process is going well. Speaking just for myself, and not wanting to backseat playtest (or worse, backseat write!), I'm genuinely excited about some of the new ideas I've seen that weren't present in the original - such as the idea of a mechanic based on Unleashing from DA:Fae. I just also want it to still feel like a Changeling game, with the core setting ideas still intact, rather than a chance to write a new game &quot;inspired by&quot;. <br /> <br /> Sounds like that's what you guys want too, though, and I'm really excited to see that you've got a job freelancing for it. I've been at the very peripheries of Changeling fandom since the original WW boards went down, but stuff like KB: Boggans even I took notice of, and really appreciated you guys making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T05:38:42-07:00","id":892440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892428#post892428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just also want it to still feel like a Changeling game, with the core setting ideas still intact, rather than a chance to write a new game &quot;inspired by&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike V20, W20, and M20, C20 is going to be a true 3rd edition along with being an anniversary edition. Pretty much all of the mechanics, including the seemings, are getting tweaked at least a little bit. The goal, though, is to get to the heart of Changeling: The Dreaming and really make everything build to the core themes of the game. Everyone involved is a huge fan of Changeling: The Dreaming. Lost and DA: Fae are great games, but they're not Changeling: The Dreaming. We all want to make this the Dreamingest edition of Dreaming that's ever been Dreamed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One thing I will say about seemings - in my first play test session I was lucky enough to have all of my original players from back when we all first discovered Changeling: The Dreaming together in one place again. We all remade our very first Changeling characters using the C20 play test documents. Back in the day, all of these characters were wilders, but this was the first time I've ever had a childling, wilder, and grump all as PCs in the same group. It was glorious!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-17-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T13:14:08-07:00","id":892728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892440#post892440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unlike V20, W20, and M20, C20 is going to be a true 3rd edition along with being an anniversary edition. Pretty much all of the mechanics, including the seemings, are getting tweaked at least a little bit. The goal, though, is to get to the heart of Changeling: The Dreaming and really make everything build to the core themes of the game. Everyone involved is a huge fan of Changeling: The Dreaming. Lost and DA: Fae are great games, but they're not Changeling: The Dreaming. We all want to make this the Dreamingest edition of Dreaming that's ever been Dreamed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One thing I will say about seemings - in my first play test session I was lucky enough to have all of my original players from back when we all first discovered Changeling: The Dreaming together in one place again. We all remade our very first Changeling characters using the C20 play test documents. Back in the day, all of these characters were wilders, but this was the first time I've ever had a childling, wilder, and grump all as PCs in the same group. It was glorious!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, we never got a proper revised edition, which was always a real shame. That and the Book of Glamour. I adore the magic system, it has some of the openness and creativity of Mage but without stepping on that game's toes and while maintaining a great, off-kilter feel. But it would really have benefited from a clean-up pass and tidy-up. As you say, DA: Fae and Lost were great games, and for many people, I'm sure, better than Changeling, but... Yeah. I've loved it since I was barely more than a Childling, and I'm now a long way into my Grump years and I've yet to find any game I love quite as much.<br /> <br /> Also thanks for the teasers about the playtesting. We're currently running an epic, All-Bard D&amp;D Planescape game, but our group has agreed, once that's over, we really need to revisit Changeling either with the new 20th Anniversary edition, or in preparation for it. I get that sometimes it can be challenging, but I've always found mixing the seemings to be great fun too. It adds a really interesting additional element with regards to mortal society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-17-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:21:02-07:00","id":892772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892425#post892425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So yeah, I think representing that with age is fairer than doing so with any other attribute, because unlike race, gender, economic status, etc., aging is universal.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a perfectly good mechanic for how much your dream has died. Its called Banality. Letting it decide how much it has won and lost over your life time up to the start of the game should be up to the player. I want the tragedy of 7 year old &quot;grumps&quot; and the triumph of 50 year old &quot;childlings&quot;. I want the Siochan(sp) to be a big and serious thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:44:22-07:00","id":892793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892772#post892772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have a perfectly good mechanic for how much your dream has died. Its called Banality. Letting it decide how much it has won and lost over your life time up to the start of the game should be up to the player. I want the tragedy of 7 year old &quot;grumps&quot; and the triumph of 50 year old &quot;childlings&quot;. I want the Siochan(sp) to be a big and serious thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I've said, I think we can represent both undone Childlings and Grumps who live vibrant, dream-filled lives with the current mechanics too, and I think the job of the mechanics is to underscore the broader trends of the setting. Obviously exceptions exist and the golden rule, and house rules, can and should be used where appropriate, which will be a decision for each individual gaming group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:18:13-07:00","id":892905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892772#post892772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have a perfectly good mechanic for how much your dream has died. Its called Banality. Letting it decide how much it has won and lost over your life time up to the start of the game should be up to the player. I want the tragedy of 7 year old &quot;grumps&quot; and the triumph of 50 year old &quot;childlings&quot;. I want the Siochan(sp) to be a big and serious thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also pretty much what I'd be interested in, although I don't know if I necessarily see it through the lens of tragedy and triumph. I see Grumpdom as a sort of adaptation you have to make in order to reconcile your Changeling nature with the loss of innocence the demands of the mortal world. Is it unfortunate that a child would already be a Grump? Quite possibly, but it depends on the circumstances. By the same token, an adult Childling would be a precarious tightrope to walk. Admirable? Quite possibly, but undertaken only by someone with obsessive dedication to the Changeling ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:37:14-07:00","id":892922,"title":"","content":"I think the seemings are integral to the setting. Tying them to age generally makes sense (although I think the age ranges shouldn't be concrete). Those very dramatic exceptions (grumps who are seven years old) should probably be handled with Merits and Flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:54:58-07:00","id":892932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892793#post892793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as I've said, I think we can represent both undone Childlings and Grumps who live vibrant, dream-filled lives with the current mechanics too, and I think the job of the mechanics is to underscore the broader trends of the setting. Obviously exceptions exist and the golden rule, and house rules, can and should be used where appropriate, which will be a decision for each individual gaming group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have never found Seeming particularly integral to the chararacters. Either someone took a particular set up for power gaming reasons or for astetic reasons. Seeming has always come off as arbitrary in my experience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:12:03-07:00","id":893459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=892922#post892922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the seemings are integral to the setting. Tying them to age generally makes sense (although I think the age ranges shouldn't be concrete). Those very dramatic exceptions (grumps who are seven years old) should probably be handled with Merits and Flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I would agree with this. I don't think the age boundaries should be ironclad either (particularly considering the disconnect between mortal age and chronological age for characters who spend time in the Dreaming or Freeholds), and I would also not be against Merits/Flaws to express unusual starting stats. <br /> <br /> I suppose to compare it to other WoD games, it feels analogous to me to the notion that Vampires inevitably lose their humanity. Obviously there will be exceptions and pursuing the opportunity to <i>be</i> the exception is likely to be a big motivating factor for many characters. But the mechanics, broadly speaking, describe the currents of the world. Even if our goal is to swim against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:22:53-07:00","id":893833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=893459#post893459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I would agree with this. I don't think the age boundaries should be ironclad either (particularly considering the disconnect between mortal age and chronological age for characters who spend time in the Dreaming or Freeholds), and I would also not be against Merits/Flaws to express unusual starting stats.<br /> <br /> I suppose to compare it to other WoD games, it feels analogous to me to the notion that Vampires inevitably lose their humanity. Obviously there will be exceptions and pursuing the opportunity to <i>be</i> the exception is likely to be a big motivating factor for many characters. But the mechanics, broadly speaking, describe the currents of the world. Even if our goal is to swim against them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except there's no mechanic for forcing your vampire to start the game at a certain humanity/path level except prioritizing it over other things. There's no mechanic to support any of this. All there is is different Humours levels based on age and certain kiths get bonuses when they hit 30. Hell there's no mechanic for even switching from seeming to seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:32:49-07:00","id":894281,"title":"","content":"Actually the mechanics for switching from seeming to seeming are called The Togail an Ainm and are described at page 50 from The Enchanted.<br /> <br /> I think Seemings are essencial to the core concept that makes Changeling: the Dreaming not other fae-themed game. I hope from the bottom of my heart that they keep the idea that time corrodes the fragile faerie soul. I think it's a beautiful and poetic concept, probably inherited from J. M. Barrie, that forces us to be aware that even if you keep a young body, you cannot be young forever because your mind remembers all the time you lived, unless you're like Peter Pan and forgets everything you live constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:08:13-07:00","id":894436,"title":"","content":"I guess, for me, it's about inevitability. Most of the other games were dark in quite obvious ways, but Changeling was often subtle. Tying Seemings to age means that the fall to Banality is pretty much inevitable. As you age, you will be Undone eventually. Detaching Seemings from age, or at least the passage of time, diminishes that sense of inevitability. It's not definite that you'll be Undone, because there are now Childlings who are 25, 50, 75 or even older. Previously, such beings would have been flukes or extra special snowflakes; instead they'd become far more commonplace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:22:18-07:00","id":894450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894281#post894281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the mechanics for switching from seeming to seeming are called The Togail an Ainm and are described at page 50 from The Enchanted.<br /> <br /> I think Seemings are essencial to the core concept that makes Changeling: the Dreaming not other fae-themed game. I hope from the bottom of my heart that they keep the idea that time corrodes the fragile faerie soul. I think it's a beautiful and poetic concept, probably inherited from J. M. Barrie, that forces us to be aware that even if you keep a young body, you cannot be young forever because your mind remembers all the time you lived, unless you're like Peter Pan and forgets everything you live constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something that's essential to the core should not be off in a suppliment. I'd also argue the game was the exact opposite you held onto your dream and didn't forget it didn't age you. Forgetting was a price of aging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:51:25-07:00","id":894539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894450#post894450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Something that's essential to the core should not be off in a suppliment. I'd also argue the game was the exact opposite you held onto your dream and didn't forget it didn't age you. Forgetting was a price of aging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Forgetting *is* a price of ageing. Hence why older characters *should*, generally, have more Banality. Hence, Seemings that are tied to age brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T22:41:38-07:00","id":894568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894436#post894436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, for me, it's about inevitability. Most of the other games were dark in quite obvious ways, but Changeling was often subtle. Tying Seemings to age means that the fall to Banality is pretty much inevitable. As you age, you will be Undone eventually. Detaching Seemings from age, or at least the passage of time, diminishes that sense of inevitability. It's not definite that you'll be Undone, because there are now Childlings who are 25, 50, 75 or even older. Previously, such beings would have been flukes or extra special snowflakes; instead they'd become far more commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most vampires don't make it out of 50 years, there's a reason there are few old werewolves, and there's more bricks in Stygia than people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894539#post894539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Forgetting *is* a price of ageing. Hence why older characters *should*, generally, have more Banality. Hence, Seemings that are tied to age brackets.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 7 yearold with banality 7 is closer to undoing than 65 yearold with banality 5. For all the talk of treating them differently the game really doesn't. the ability to play a banality 3 30 yearold should be possible it should just come at a price. Just like if I want to to tell the story of the death of childhood in a pure childhood setting that should also be an option. Just like I can choose to play a humanity 8 vampire or a humanity 5 to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:06:59-07:00","id":894832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894568#post894568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the ability to play a banality 3 30 yearold should be possible it should just come at a price. Just like if I want to to tell the story of the death of childhood in a pure childhood setting that should also be an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what should the price be? As I've said, I'm not against the idea of there being specific merits or flaws that shift these boundaries, or for specific STs to houserule things in ways that work for their stories or groups. And there <i>is </i>a core mechanic for reducing permanent banality - it's noted to be possible through the completion of epic quests and triumphs. I also always assumed the starting banality of wilders and grumps referred to an average - how much most Changelings would have accumulated by then. A 30 year old noble who has refused to leave his Freehold in years might well still have a banality of 3 (and probably be at higher risk of Bedlam than being Undone). Likewise a truly heroic grump, who has completed many heroic quests may have succeeded in reducing her banality and keeping it low. <br /> <br /> If you are creating NPCs, there is no need to adhere to the starting stats, and if you want to play a player character which doesn't stick to them either, then that should be a conversation between you and your Storyteller. If you want to tell a story of children trapped in awful conditions and agree that everyone will play childling characters, but begin with grump tempers to reflect the specific atmosphere and environment of the campaign, power to you. Themed campaigns can be really affecting and engaging.<br /> <br /> The setting and the mechanics that describe the setting are designed to be tools that establish the world in its most common configurations. This means that where dramatically appropriate they can be inverted, or subverted to great effect. But that is also possible because they establish the thematic baseline in the first place. <br /> <br /> In this case, that the world wears on the faerie soul, and the longer you are in it, the greater the struggle. <br /> <br /> So we come back to that 30 year old character with a banality of 3. What <i>should </i>the price be? Decoupling age from seeming means that there will be no price, it's player choice at no price. It ceases to be unusual. It ceases to be triumphant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:58:06-07:00","id":894975,"title":"","content":"I'm really glad that i'm not alone in what I think that makes CtD this beautiful, melancholic and fragile game. Thank you, people! &lt;3<br /> <br /> All changes coming from the 20th Anniversary Edition are welcome, since they don't destroy the game concept. And even if these rules that could change its concept, they could be there, presented as optional rules, since there're people that doesn't like the same aspects of the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T21:14:45-07:00","id":895277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=894832#post894832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what should the price be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Determined by character creation, you buy up or buy down Banality from a base point make it a simple matter of character creation than some sort of optional special snowflake merit system.<br /> <br /> <br /> The more I've thought about this thread I think Banality in general has been done wrong. Its treated generally as an active thing, something you generally get in play, much like humanity loss in vampire. However they are sort of inverted situations really, a vampire creates a stagnant routine because that won't risk their morality. Going out to &quot;Adventure&quot; is when they risk change they risk their carefully built morality in the face of the beast. Conversely for the changeling the risk isn't when they go out and adventure the risk for banality is when they fall into routines, that perhaps there should be some sort of mechanic for determining background Banality the Pc picks for interacting with the mundane world. I think this might cover both my side and your side of the issue. As this would more readily cover much of the fluff dangers of grumpdom that just never showed up in the mechanics, but also allow those who cheat the system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T03:41:47-07:00","id":896008,"title":"","content":"That's an idea I could get behind in a lot of ways. As I said I wouldn't be against it as a Merit/Flaw situation, so a point buy could work. Though as I've said my view is that there needs to be a mechanical correlation between growing older and gaining banality to establish underlying themes, so I think it'd need to be a point-buy from differing baselines. Like as a Grump your default banality is 5, but with an option to buy it down with freebies. Or if you want to be a Childling with a higher banality, there could be an &quot;increased banality&quot; flaw based a more difficult pre-chronicle life. I think it should be a reasonably expensive one though because banality should be a big deal and buying it off - or accepting extra - should be a big deal too.<br /> <br /> That way you give options to players who want to play against type without undercutting the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T20:33:47-07:00","id":896491,"title":"","content":"I've never derived normality from player builds vs Npcs. Or there'd be no nongrump trolls(those 2 strength they call!). But really more when thinking about how the Tempers develop a setting. As it is Banality 5 can cover a long hard life or a semester with the wrong teacher. I think something that covers the aspects of your life and the dangers they are to your dream would help better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T16:03:19-07:00","id":897289,"title":"","content":"I think Time should be the biggest variable in this equation yet. Even if you live a happy and creative life, you cannot overcome banality, because it's noxious and it saturates our atmosphere. Reality corrodes everything magic and even if you manage years and years fighting against it, you're going to loose in the end. That's the horror in CtD and what makes it the saddest WoD game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That's why I like the seemings and think it's important to the concept of CtD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:51:31-07:00","id":897427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=897289#post897289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Time should be the biggest variable in this equation yet. Even if you live a happy and creative life, you cannot overcome banality, because it's noxious and it saturates our atmosphere. Reality corrodes everything magic and even if you manage years and years fighting against it, you're going to loose in the end. That's the horror in CtD and what makes it the saddest WoD game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That's why I like the seemings and think it's important to the concept of CtD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except they don't? Grump is.. actually pretty sweet starting point. Your banality isn't crushing. Its enough to be a decent defense against anyone throwing Cantrips at you, and certain kiths get bonuses for it. Actually in my experiences starting with More banality meant the player was MUCH more careful, the &quot;Grump&quot; went out of their way to not have issues while the childlings and wilders quickly caught up.<br /> <br /> Banality should be crushing and dangerous and starting tempers just doesn't do that. Perhaps having some mechanic by which they get glamour or banality might mean something more though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:51:06-07:00","id":898121,"title":"","content":"I think starting tempers do that. In my experience as a Storyteller no player wants to be a Grump, I think it's because (at least in my CtD games) banality is a real menace. So, the less your starting Banality, the longer your character interacts with the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I'm really fond of a rule presented in Vampire: the Dark Ages (that one before Dark Ages line): every changeling gets 1 permanent Banality point for every 7 years living as a Changeling. It kind of corroborates with the seeming's starting Banality (1 from 0-7 years old, 3 from 14-21 years old and 5 from 28-35 years old) and pushes farther the concept of Time spent here as noxious to changeling's fragile souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:06:54-07:00","id":898133,"title":"","content":"I go back and forth on this just about every time I think about it. On the one hand the inevitability of being poisoned by Banality and the Grump's dilemma is central to my conception of the game. You either resign yourself to fading away gracefully, eaten by the spiritual cancer you know your best efforts will never be enough to stop, or you commit yourself to keeping your fae soul alive by any means necessary, no matter who you have to hurt to do it. That is Changeling. That is what brought me to the game and keeps me coming back. On the other hand the whole system just seems kind of arbitrary and can't help but feel particularly inflected by the Gen X sensibilities that birthed it, even compared to the rest of the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:25:30-07:00","id":898217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=898121#post898121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think starting tempers do that. In my experience as a Storyteller no player wants to be a Grump, I think it's because (at least in my CtD games) banality is a real menace. So, the less your starting Banality, the longer your character interacts with the Dreaming.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>My experiences were the exact opposite No one wanted to play a Wilder. childlings had the Glamour Grumps had the Wp and I never saw a Troll who wasn't a grump. Those who did pick wilders burnt out quickly while childlings at least had 2 less points of banality to learn to game the system while anyone who picked grump clearly seemed to grasp how to do it. Finding that proper balance is also a theme of the game even if the legendary Sichain(sp) never got any proper development asside from &quot;here's this immortal guy who's done it!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly I think this may be a matter of player interaction. Those of us who see it as arbitrary never got anything out of the mechanic while those who did, well did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 05-24-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:18:41-07:00","id":898939,"title":"","content":"If in your game people care more about extra Strength or Willpower points and not what kind of character they want to be, well, I think you should play D&amp;D with your friends, it's also really fun! Or you can explore better the game atmosphere and involve more your players inside the game's reality. Nothing in WoD games are really balanced only looking at the rules, you should be involved by the scenary to have more fun and enjoy the game. I'm not telling there's a right or wrong way to play WoD games, I'm just saying how you can accept the core elements from this game and still have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:25:22-07:00","id":899086,"title":"","content":"Please let's not trot out the old &quot;role-play vs roll-play&quot; arguments. They're tired, they need a rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:01:58-07:00","id":899499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=898939#post898939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If in your game people care more about extra Strength or Willpower points and not what kind of character they want to be, well, I think you should play D&amp;D with your friends, it's also really fun! Or you can explore better the game atmosphere and involve more your players inside the game's reality. Nothing in WoD games are really balanced only looking at the rules, you should be involved by the scenary to have more fun and enjoy the game. I'm not telling there's a right or wrong way to play WoD games, I'm just saying how you can accept the core elements from this game and still have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe being strong of will and strong of body is an important part of the character? I know its crazy but maybe people are drawn to playing Trolls because they want to be large strong guy of unbending will and purpose? I know its crazy to try and use mechanics to represent our characters rather than blindly play without them(and for some reason give Onyx path/white wolf money for these mechanics we should deign to never look at)<br /> <br /> you say the breaks in seeming promote a certain play style. I'm disagreeing. I've never seen someone pick grump as &quot;dead man walking&quot; but the &quot;i've tangled with banality plenty of times and maybe I have my scars but I've won!&quot; I've seen people who try to play WIlder and childlings from the description who were far more &quot;dead man walking&quot; running head long into Banality without thought and direction because they don't have the tools to back things up.<br /> <br /> So I'm saying again Seeming has not served to promote core elements of the game. It has come to me to be purely arbitrary, but this I think is an outgrowth of Banality being fairly poorly defined. A stronger banality system would better help with supporting the themes and moods of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T23:21:45-07:00","id":901799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=898939#post898939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If in your game people care more about extra Strength or Willpower points and not what kind of character they want to be, well, I think you should play D&amp;D with your friends, it's also really fun! Or you can explore better the game atmosphere and involve more your players inside the game's reality. Nothing in WoD games are really balanced only looking at the rules, you should be involved by the scenary to have more fun and enjoy the game. <b>I'm not telling there's a right or wrong way to play WoD games</b>, I'm just saying how you can accept the core elements from this game and still have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Except you did in your very first sentence. Please don't do that again, it doesn't lead to constructive conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:49:24-07:00","id":903814,"title":"","content":"This sort of threads really do take me back to the &quot;Good Ol' Days&quot; of the old changeling forum. <br /> One of the things i most enjoyed about this game was that there were so many gaps in the rules, and that the fans took it upon themselves to come up with house-rules to fill in such gaps. Some of those house rules were amazing. There were others that were merely adecuate. Of course there were also the awful ideas, but lets not dwell on that. In a way, the gaps in the rules were an integral part of the game.a<br /> <br /> So what if we didn't get a Rev. Edition, we just came up with fun ideas to cope.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the topic at hand... At first, when i saw the Wonder/Seeker/Keeper bit i was surprised. A new mechanic that would affect the game at the most basic of levels. At first I was against it... but then i changed my mind (i do that. A lot) We need to wait until further teasers reveal a bit more about this new mechanic. I will most likely come to love the idea once my troupe has had a chance to play the game... But even if i don't, there's nothing to worry about. I will simply hit it with the old &quot;house-ruling-stick&quot; until it fits into something my players will enjoy.<br /> <br /> That's the beauty of Changeling, that Glamour and Creativity are not only for our characters to enjoy and use.<br /> <br /> <br /> Signed by Loumen<br /> (now a Grump who has had the time to come to terms with it - whether it be tied to his age-bracket or not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:08:25-07:00","id":903899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=903814#post903814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of threads really do take me back to the &quot;Good Ol' Days&quot; of the old changeling forum.<br /> One of the things i most enjoyed about this game was that there were so many gaps in the rules, and that the fans took it upon themselves to come up with house-rules to fill in such gaps. Some of those house rules were amazing. There were others that were merely adecuate. Of course there were also the awful ideas, but lets not dwell on that. In a way, the gaps in the rules were an integral part of the game.a<br /> <br /> So what if we didn't get a Rev. Edition, we just came up with fun ideas to cope.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the topic at hand... At first, when i saw the Wonder/Seeker/Keeper bit i was surprised. A new mechanic that would affect the game at the most basic of levels. At first I was against it... but then i changed my mind (i do that. A lot) We need to wait until further teasers reveal a bit more about this new mechanic. I will most likely come to love the idea once my troupe has had a chance to play the game... But even if i don't, there's nothing to worry about. I will simply hit it with the old &quot;house-ruling-stick&quot; until it fits into something my players will enjoy.<br /> <br /> That's the beauty of Changeling, that Glamour and Creativity are not only for our characters to enjoy and use.<br /> <br /> <br /> Signed by Loumen<br /> (now a Grump who has had the time to come to terms with it - whether it be tied to his age-bracket or not)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd prefer to not spend 150 or so dollars on something I have to house rule heavily to get to the themes they are trying to portray. I can always freeform with a bunch of friends mechanics should enhanable and help us build a story vs being a horrific thing we must ignore to &quot;Really roleplay&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:27:18-07:00","id":903908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=903899#post903899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd prefer to not spend 150 or so dollars on something I have to house rule heavily to get to the themes they are trying to portray. I can always freeform with a bunch of friends mechanics should enhanable and help us build a story vs being a horrific thing we must ignore to &quot;Really roleplay&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true for C20. Although, I'll admit, half the fun I had with Second Edition was coming up with ways to fill the gaps. But yeah, I've done that now, so I'd like a C20 that works off the bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-31-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:55:48-07:00","id":903914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=903908#post903908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true for C20. Although, I'll admit, half the fun I had with Second Edition was coming up with ways to fill the gaps. But yeah, I've done that now, so I'd like a V20 that works off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I played Scion, that killed my &quot;forge a game into playabliity&quot; That and there's so many more options now. Plus I'd rather see more kiths, arts etc than &quot;Here's the 35th attempt to make Banality work..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:42:06-07:00","id":904364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=903914#post903914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I played Scion, that killed my &amp;quot;forge a game into playabliity&amp;quot; That and there's so many more options now. Plus I'd rather see more kiths, arts etc than &amp;quot;Here's the 35th attempt to make Banality work..&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Word.<br /> <br /> Plus, there can never be enough kiths for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:18:37-07:00","id":908652,"title":"","content":"Clearly English is not my first language, so I may have been misunderstood. I wasn't saying that you cannot play CtD the way you have more fun, you can do whatever you want, my first sentence was just suggesting another game that has more rules and options to this theme and mood, so you can have MORE fun with that. You can also be an epic character (or just a little stronger/smarter/etc) in a WoD game, you don't even need to change the rules, just ask for more freebie points at your character creation and voil\u00e1: you can have a strong willed and resistant troll or anything you want.<br /> My only point here is: you can ALSO have fun with all those things as they were presented in the books. I can understand that your players don't see the Seemings as something organic or part of the core concepts of this game, ok, so I am just suggesting that you can make them more involved with the world presented. It worked very well in my games, I am a CtD storyteller since 1998 and after some experiences, I learned how to make my players involved in this world and since then never, EVER, a player has choosen a Seeming for nothing except to complete the character's concept. I am just trying to help you as I share my experiences and points of view. I've already experienced tons of problems in CtD games, VtM games, etc. I think that C20 will bring a more complete approach of Glamour x Banality and what these things mean, so, I guess this would help the Seemings to be something more complex and maybe more appealing for you and your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:42:46-07:00","id":908707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=908652#post908652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly English is not my first language, so I may have been misunderstood. I wasn't saying that you cannot play CtD the way you have more fun, you can do whatever you want, my first sentence was just suggesting another game that has more rules and options to this theme and mood, so you can have MORE fun with that. You can also be an epic character (or just a little stronger/smarter/etc) in a WoD game, you don't even need to change the rules, just ask for more freebie points at your character creation and voil\u00e1: you can have a strong willed and resistant troll or anything you want.<br /> My only point here is: you can ALSO have fun with all those things as they were presented in the books. I can understand that your players don't see the Seemings as something organic or part of the core concepts of this game, ok, so I am just suggesting that you can make them more involved with the world presented. It worked very well in my games, I am a CtD storyteller since 1998 and after some experiences, I learned how to make my players involved in this world and since then never, EVER, a player has choosen a Seeming for nothing except to complete the character's concept. I am just trying to help you as I share my experiences and points of view. I've already experienced tons of problems in CtD games, VtM games, etc. I think that C20 will bring a more complete approach of Glamour x Banality and what these things mean, so, I guess this would help the Seemings to be something more complex and maybe more appealing for you and your players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Asking for more points is changing the rules. The Troll theme is a person who is strong of body and will. A Creature as unbending as the mountains. That is their dream that is their concept. The mechanics in this game use strength and willpower to represent these things. The mechanics are there to represent the character. If I just want to freeform through things I can. I don't need the mechanics at all to tell a collective story, but if I am using rules those rules should be in an aid in directing the situation vs &quot;just throw things out and work with the fluff&quot;<br /> <br /> That is my complaint about Seemings. They don't seem to really do anything. Presumably there should be some difference between the banality 5 childling and the banality 5 Grump.. but there isn't more so the Grump has a much stronger sense of self(represented by willpower). I am not against Seemings perse but I'd like a better point than what is presented. Seeming once you start the game mechanically has few effects, I'd prefer to see it have a continuous effect vs all being frontloaded on Tempers. I'd also prefer kiths not have an obvious best Seeming match up like I hit at with Trolls, a Troll childling completely loses one of his Birthrights, my concept of being the biggest strongest childling is unreallizable, the Pooka or SIdhe, or Sluagh can be just as strong as me! Meanwhile the Sidhe childling is just as glorious as any elder. Yes I can change the rules. I could run stat caps for childlings, but if I need to fix something that proves its a failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:09:37-07:00","id":908799,"title":"","content":"Considering the starting character points you are already superior to most of the humanity. I think that Changelings are just a pale reflection of what they once were. IMHO the rules can cover it most of the time.<br /> So, specifically about the Trolls, I agree with you. They should have made Childlings physically strong in some aspect (not sure an extra dot of Str, but certainly something). Even so, this doesn't invalidate the Seeming concept and how Time spent here corrodes the fae nature.<br /> I think that instead of ignore something that could be nice and explored during the chronicles, it's better to ask for a more complete approach about Seemings, Aging, Banality and Glamour to these things turn more appealing and organic to your game and everyone not satisfied with the information given until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:33:46-07:00","id":908810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=908799#post908799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the starting character points you are already superior to most of the humanity. I think that Changelings are just a pale reflection of what they once were. IMHO the rules can cover it most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its in comparison to other fae. Should a troll be stronger than a Sluagh? Should a Sidhe be more glorious than a Redcap? Should a pooka be better able to turn into a bear than a Nocker?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, specifically about the Trolls, I agree with you. They should have made Childlings physically strong in some aspect (not sure an extra dot of Str, but certainly something). Even so, this doesn't invalidate the Seeming concept and how Time spent here corrodes the fae nature.<br /> I think that instead of ignore something that could be nice and explored during the chronicles, it's better to ask for a more complete approach about Seemings, Aging, Banality and Glamour to these things turn more appealing and organic to your game and everyone not satisfied with the information given until now. </div> </div> </div>I am saying that Seeming currently does nothing but define your Tempers and give you bonuses for certain Kiths. I come back again to the Troll because its the most blatant counter point to the idea that a Fae fades over time, the Grump is the &quot;Most&quot; troll like, its strongest, Its most stubborn, the most suriveable etc. Grumpdom doesn't represent a fading for the Troll but rather fully getting ones birth right.<br /> <br /> Tempers on the other hand can readily be changed in game. a Grump doesn't have it any harder increasing his glamour than anything else. Quests can and do reduce banality. I am not saying this how the game SHOULD be but rather as it is. There needs to be a better way because right now Seeming at best comes off as arbitrary and at worse is counter to any concept of the Fae fading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T01:03:54-07:00","id":908971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=908810#post908810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its in comparison to other fae. Should a troll be stronger than a Sluagh? Should a Sidhe be more glorious than a Redcap? Should a pooka be better able to turn into a bear than a Nocker?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am saying that Seeming currently does nothing but define your Tempers and give you bonuses for certain Kiths. I come back again to the Troll because its the most blatant counter point to the idea that a Fae fades over time, the Grump is the &amp;quot;Most&amp;quot; troll like, its strongest, Its most stubborn, the most suriveable etc. Grumpdom doesn't represent a fading for the Troll but rather fully getting ones birth right.<br /> <br /> Tempers on the other hand can readily be changed in game. a Grump doesn't have it any harder increasing his glamour than anything else. Quests can and do reduce banality. I am not saying this how the game SHOULD be but rather as it is. There needs to be a better way because right now Seeming at best comes off as arbitrary and at worse is counter to any concept of the Fae fading.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game has always been about such contradictions. A troll whose birthrights grow stronger even as his Banality also grows is very thematically appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T02:21:58-07:00","id":908996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=908971#post908971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game has always been about such contradictions. A troll whose birthrights grow stronger even as his Banality also grows is very thematically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not that he goes stronger perse though that reflects the situation its that a Troll is most.. archtypally Troll at Grump. He is the best representation of being a Troll at that level vs having faded from a Fae childling. Now we can say all sorts of things about why this is, but if a theme is the Fading of Fairy nature in the onslaught of years the eldest shouldn't be the MOST archtypal representation of the kith.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:27:05-07:00","id":910326,"title":"","content":"Actually I tend to agree with you about the Trolls (partially). I've never thought about them this way. Thanks.<br /> But, on the other side, I don't see the same about the other kiths. I insist: the writers should explore more the Seemings, Glamour and Banality (and I think they've had planned it, but the Book of Glamour never came to the light). Maybe they should do something about how troll's birthrights work, as they did in their Nocker's preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:08:44-07:00","id":910410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891067-c20-wonder-seeker-keeper?p=910326#post910326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I tend to agree with you about the Trolls (partially). I've never thought about them this way. Thanks.<br /> But, on the other side, I don't see the same about the other kiths. I insist: the writers should explore more the Seemings, Glamour and Banality (and I think they've had planned it, but the Book of Glamour never came to the light). Maybe they should do something about how troll's birthrights work, as they did in their Nocker's preview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the only two Kiths that are expressly effected by Age. Trolls and Green Men. The only ones where being a Grump means something different than a childling with banality 5<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}